  "name": "Karcinom ovaria a tuby – diagnostická cesta",
  "name_en": "Ovarian and tubal cancer – diagnostic pathway",
  "cancer_type": "Karcinom ovaria a tuby",
  "icd_codes": [
    "C56",
    "C57"
  ],
  "summary": "From a referral with a suspicious adnexal mass to a staged patient presented at the gynaeco-oncology MDT, and the tissue diagnosis on the chosen route (primary cytoreduction or neoadjuvant chemotherapy). Ends where treatment starts. DRAFT for clinicians: requirement levels follow the binding ČOS text; imaging, markers and tissue-before-NACT come from structure sources and therefore never turn red; sla_days are placeholders.",
  "notes": [
    "The ČOS chapter (32.17) is treatment-focused. For diagnostics it binds only: staging before treatment, MDT before any treatment including surgery, fitness for curative chemotherapy, germline testing for all stages, somatic BRCA/HRD for advanced disease, optional FRα/HER2/MSI/NGS, and GI work-up + CEA for mucinous carcinoma.",
    "Expert pelvic ultrasound, CA-125/HE4, the CT extent and histology before neoadjuvant chemotherapy are NOT stated in the ČOS chapter; they come from ESMO-ESGO (cited by ČOS) and NICE and are shown as recommended. Clinicians should decide whether the KOC makes them binding (role: local).",
    "Unlike pancreas, histology usually comes from the primary operation (surgical staging); a pre-treatment biopsy is needed only on the neoadjuvant route.",
    "After neoadjuvant chemotherapy and after surgery the ČOS chapter requires another MDT – that is part of the treatment pathway, not modelled here.",
    "ČOS cites an ESGO 2026 update of the tubo-ovarian guidelines as not yet published; re-check when it appears.",
    "sla_days are local placeholders, not taken from any source."
  ],
